No DialBench data are included
  This repository contains no RPM-10K image, no label file (labels/train.json, labels/test.json), no label value and no model weights. The README of the DialBench repository lists
  the licence of the dataset and of the authors' model weights as "TBD". Anyone who wants to run the code needs the data from the authors, under whatever terms they state.
  The following files contain image FILE NAMES of the release (and block or group numbers computed by us from image similarity), nothing else of it:
  - protocol/splits_v2.json, protocol/splits_v3.json: the two re-splits (names, group or block ids, purged names).
  - predictions/*.json: the predictions of our models, one number per image name (model outputs, not labels).
  Aggregate statistics about the release (row counts, the thumbnail-similarity tables, file counts) are in docs/ and TEST-LOG.md.

Model weights
  None are included. The models were trained on RPM-10K from ImageNet-pretrained initial weights (torchvision ResNet-18, IMAGENET1K_V1, converted by kernels/model-port; timm
  MobileNetV3), which the kernels download at run time; the weights stay private until the authors state the terms for models trained on their data.

Libraries
  The code imports NumPy, PyTorch, torchvision, timm, ONNX Runtime and JAX / Flax at run time (BSD-3-Clause, Apache-2.0 and MIT licences); none of their code is included.
  src/jax_resnet.py is our own Flax implementation of ResNet-18 and ResNet-34 whose parameter names mirror torchvision's.
